# helpers stop enumerating (patch 277)
# Generated 2026-10-13
# Base: seleron/vitabrowser (patch stack through 276)
#
# Object.keys(window) and Object.getOwnPropertyNames(window) list a
# global's properties in creation order. A browser makes the ECMAScript
# intrinsics, window's attributes and operations in IDL order, its event
# handlers and interface objects, its newest APIs last; a page's globals
# follow. Fingerprinters read the tail: hCaptcha's hsw takes the
# descriptors of the last 24 keys of Object.keys(window) (in Chromium
# fetchLater, getScreenDetails, queryLocalFonts, ... then the page's own
# globals). Here the tail was whatever the bridge defined last
# (onpageshow, onpagehide, onbeforeunload, onunload, ...) -- the fork the
# hCaptcha trace hit at call 4401.
#
#  - vita_polyfill.js, last section: window's configurable own
#    properties are made again, once per realm -- the engine's own names
#    first, then the 413 that Chromium 140 also has, in Chromium's order
#    (the list in the section) -- so the tail is now ... setTimeout,
#    structuredClone, ontouchcancel ... ontouchstart, then the page's
#    globals, as in Chromium. Every property keeps its descriptor; the
#    section looks nothing up on the global while it works (Object itself
#    is taken away and put back). 2 ms of realm build on the host.
#  - DOMPurify, XF, HTML_Element, setImmediate, clearImmediate (the
#    engine's, no web API) stop enumerating, as __vita* did in 269.
#  - fixed on the way: in the document-less realm the engine builds first,
#    the 2026-09-26 "DOM surface" section's helpers put Text's length
#    accessor on Object.prototype (a stub text node there is a plain
#    object) -- every object in that realm had a length; acc() / fn() now
#    refuse Object.prototype.
#
# With Chromium given this engine's window (names, enumerability, order),
# the hCaptcha trace now stays aligned through the walk (to call 5418,
# where the page's own globals differ); Chromium still passes, and the
# demo still refuses the engine.
#
# Gate: testpages/pages/JS-window-order.html (WINORDER 5/5, Chromium 5/5;
# the build before fails 1-3).
